“The app answers our life’s simplest question, “What is the most recommended thing here?”” said Tharo Sen, the co-founder and managing partner of Vrecommend, “The most recommended places or food should be shared by our closest friends. Our closest friends are people we always care about and trust, so it is going to be amazing to share every recommended experience of food and places one after another with amazing people.”
Going forward, it aims to be an affordable alternative for smaller food chains to reach a bigger pool of audience. Vrecommend has already partnered with five prominent food chains in Cambodia, including Brown Coffee and Bakery, Pizza Company and Dairy Queen.
Cambodia, with all its turbulent history and rustic charm, manages to intrigue visitors every year. Whether you’re standing in the midst of the great Angkor Wat, enjoying the serenity at the Royal Palace or feeling the waves crash against your legs at a Sihanoukville beach, we’ve round up five apps to accompany you through your journey in the Kingdom.
Our first app is for anyone who doesn’t understand Khmer, Cambodia’s national language. Google Translate allows you to take pictures of foreign text and helps you translate it.
A cheeky peer-to-peer review app, Vrecommend is for tourists who are interested in what the locals like. Apart from having features that allow you to send messages and upload reviews, your feed can be personalised to suit your preferences as well.
Discover Cambodia is an app for those looking for culture and a little luxury. The only magazine app that offers high quality pictures tailored just for Cambodia, Discover Cambodia boasts articles and photographs from some of the best writers and photographers.
This one is for the foreigners interested in immersing themselves like locals. EZECOM, an Internet Provider from Cambodia, has an app that allows you to listen to the Kingdom’s local radio stations.
