Cambodia’s fastest growing career portal that has already commenced operation in 7 other countries – Sri Lanka, Myanmar, Cameroom, Bangladesh, Uganda, Ivory Coast, and Senegal, has now launched the platform in Khmer, making it easier for the Cambodian population to access a wide-range of job opportunities.
Co-Founder and Managing Director of the site, Anne Rose Dingermans shared that this enhances not only the overall experience of job seekers but employers as well by catering to the language that they are most comfortable with. The new translation enables registration, posting of job listings and the browsing of more than 3,300 career opportunities in Khmer.
Creating your own CV with the site’s tool, a user-friendly site navigation, enhanced search filters and even better, professional career advice, which is of paramount importance when it comes to job-hunting. By integrating the Khmer language into a job portal, Everjobs’ goal is to help any talented job seeker to find the right career that matches their individual skills.
