In partnership with Development Innovations, EPIC is a 1 year program that will invest in and support early-stage entrepreneurs and startups to launch and grow their businesses. This scheme will be the first of its kind in the Kingdom to invest up to USD$20,000 in 5 exceptional social startups.
Applications have been opened since 29th August, and interested parties will have to send in their technology based, impact focused ideas by 23rd September this year.
Teams will then have to pitch their ideas at a Demo Day, and only 5 teams will be chosen to move on to the acceleration phase.
Commencing in January next year, the selected teams will work with business mentors for 36 weeks in order to accelerate their startups. The USD $20,000 investment will include resources for rapid prototyping, stipends, workspaces, and consultation sessions.
The acceleration phase will end on a final Demo Day, where the 5 teams will pitch their startups to an audience consisting of potential investors and grant givers. After Demo Day ends, Impact Hub will still continue to provide support to these teams, in order to help them grow and scale their impact.
