Just to refresh your memory, CICTA is an annual national awards program, where only the most exceptional individuals, governments, and private organisations who have greatly assisted in the advancement of Cambodia’s Information and Communication Technology industry will be awarded. In our previous article, we gave you the timeline of the awards program, where we also mentioned the final selection and award ceremony.
The application process is really simple; all you need do is complete these 3 steps:
The company must be locally registered in Cambodia, OR
In the case of joint ventures (JVs) between a local and a foreign company outside of Cambodia, it doesn’t matter if the JV company is registered in or outside of Cambodia, as long as the shareholders in Cambodia hold at least 51% of the shares.
The product’s Intellectual Property (IP) rights must be owned by a company that meets the company eligibility criteria, OR
At least 51% of the product’s development efforts, including research and development as well as design, must have been done in Cambodia
How did the Cambodia ICT Awards event come about?
If you’re still unclear about anything / have any questions, feel free to check out CICTA’s official website here.
Don’t miss out on this great opportunity to win one of the most coveted awards in Cambodia’s ICT sector!
Other than that, the awards will also provide local individuals and organisations in Cambodia with the chance to spark innovation, creativity, and motivation in the ICT sector.
Public Sector: made up of public sector related ICT products (e.g e-Government)
Corporate Social Responsibility: made up of ICT products that back up the community with the goal of advocating rights and needs of certain people, or products that enhance the community’s wellbeing or aspect of life, with the eventual goal of bringing the gap closer between the digital divide
Winners from each category of award will receive a prize certificate, trophy, and monetary prizes in relation to their respective winning places. The 1st place winner will receive USD$1000, while the runner-up will receive USD$500, followed by $USD300 for the second-runner up.
