]]> Generally Trade Balance / Balance of Trade (BoT) is the difference between the difference between the total number of export products and services from a country with a total product and services imported into a country.
Bot is the largest component in the preparation of the Balance of Payment or Current Account, which is the real amount of the financial condition / treasury of the state.
If in a country domestic demand (import) larger than the export of products and services, then the BoT will show a negative number, which is then referred to as the Trade Deficit.
Nah, every country would want his country's trade balance is always positive because it means the country's economic growth to do more good for export rather than import.
Countries with large trade deficits are essentially borrowing money from citizens and / or the international community to purchase goods and services in order to meet domestic demand.
