ADB is an official Google tool for use in Android development and the flashing process. ADB stands for Android Debug Bridge and this tool basically allows you to establish a connection between your phone and a computer so you can communicate with the two devices.
Basic ADB Commands:
adb devices Shows you a list of devices that are attached to the PC
adb install<ApplicationpathPackagename>.apk ADB allows for the installation of APK files directly on a phone. If you type in this command and hit the enter key, ADB will begin installing the app on the phone.
