Note 4 was the first handset by Samsung to leave the plastic body, it had its charisma but Note 5 has already tipped the scale toward itself in the design category.
On the front and rear of Note 5 there is a Gorilla Glass covering, the backplate is shiny. It is a perfect example of modern aesthetics.
Note 4 does not have a shiny surface but unlike Note 5 it is not a fingerprint magnet.
The button position on the edges is the same on both phablets.
Volume rocker button is on the left edge for both device. Note 5 has separate volume buttons while Note 4 has a single rocker button.
There is a rounded rectangular button beneath the screen for Home function. This button has a fingerprint scanner incorporated into it on both devices.
One of the biggest advantages of Note 4 is that it has a removable back cover, removable battery and a slot for microSD card.
The display of both devices is almost same.
On Note 4 there is 16 megapixels camera at the back while there is 3.7 megapixel one at the front.
Note 4 camera app has its own tweaks, dual camera, beauty face, rear cam selfie, HDR, Selective focus, Virtual tour and Panorama.
The colours calibration is almost same, in some areas Note 4 performed even better than Note 5.
In lowlight conditions Note 4 gives better colours.
The performance of Note 5 is remarkable super fast and super smooth.
The graphic unit of Note 5 is a little more advanced as compared to Note 4.
Note 4 comes in only the 32GB version but it has a micro SD card slot that can support a card of up to 128 GB.
The total screen on time for Note 5 is 9 hours and 11 minutes, which is much more than its predecessor Note 4.
Browsing experience is great on both devices.
Note 5 has a few new feature related to stylus for example you can write notes even when the screen is off, you can’t do this with Note 4. Verdict
Note 4 has the advantage of removable battery and microSD while the design of Note 5 is certainly more premium. The performance of Note 5 is better, camera of both devices is equal, display is also on equal grounds but the battery life of Note 5 is more dependable.
