Chemical and engineering materials company 5N Plus has announced the launch of a new metal powder-scandium metal powder product portfolio to enter the 3D printing market.
According to 5N Plus, its goal is to become a leading engineered powder supplier in the 3D printing industry.
Since its establishment, 5N Plus has accumulated experience and learned lessons from the smaller technically challenging market it initially entered, and then decided to expand its functionality. In the past three years, the company has secured multiple plans in the handheld electronic device platform due to its investment in a high-performance spherical powder product portfolio.
For the additive manufacturing market, 5N Plus has developed a new product portfolio of engineered powders based on copper and copper-based alloys. These materials are engineered with optimized structures to show controlled oxygen content and ultra-high purity, while having uniform surface oxide thickness and controlled particle size distribution.
The newly developed alloy has a higher scan content and can be heat treated and age hardened after 3D printing to improve strength and durability. At the same time, Elementum 3D, a developer of additive manufacturing materials based in Colorado, has received investment from Sumitomo Corporation (SCOA) to expand the marketing and sales of its proprietary metal powder, which combines ceramics to improve additive manufacturing performance.
