GBM working principle
The bucket flap of the grab is centered on the pin shaft of the bucket flap installed in the central cylinder. The pin shaft of the oil cylinder connected with the oil cylinder follows the oil cylinder to expand and contract, making an outward circular arc movement, and stops when the cylinder stroke limit is reached to complete the opening action.
The bucket flap of the grab is centered on the pin shaft of the bucket flap installed in the central cylinder, and the cylinder pin shaft connected to the oil cylinder follows the extension of the oil cylinder and makes an inward circular arc movement. After the bucket flap reaches full contact or encounters the rated resistance stop when the closing action is completed.
