On September 7, 2021, the first China Digital Carbon Neutrality Forum was held in Chengdu. The forum was attended by representatives from the energy industry, government departments, academics and companies to explore how digital tools can be used effectively to help achieve the goal of “peaking CO2 emissions by 2030 and achieving carbon neutrality by 2060″.
The forum also held three parallel sub-forums, including green and low-carbon development of digital technology enabling industries, new leap in low-carbon transformation driven by digital economy, and green and low-carbon new fashion led by digital life. At the door of the conference room of the main forum, a QR code called “Carbon neutral” caught the attention of the guests.
“Diandian Carbon Neutrality” platform is currently available for conferences, scenic spots, supermarkets, restaurants, hotels and other scenarios. It can calculate carbon emissions online, purchase carbon credits online, issue electronic certificates of honor, query carbon neutrality rankings and other functions.
